1
00:00:02,438 --> 00:00:04,356
Water.

2
00:00:04,565 --> 00:00:06,275
Earth.

3
00:00:06,567 --> 00:00:08,360
Fire.

4
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:10,612
Air.

5
00:00:10,822 --> 00:00:14,408
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,326 --> 00:00:18,370
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:21,790
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:21,874 --> 00:00:23,458
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,793 --> 00:00:26,753
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

10
00:00:27,213 --> 00:00:31,008
100 years passed, and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

11
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:32,884
an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:33,094 --> 00:00:35,137
And although his
airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,221 --> 00:00:37,681
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,807 --> 00:00:38,849
Unh!

15
00:00:38,933 --> 00:00:42,019
But I believe Aang can save the world.

16
00:01:15,303 --> 00:01:16,845
We need you, Aang.

17
00:01:17,221 --> 00:01:19,014
I need you, too.

18
00:01:24,979 --> 00:01:27,064
Be careful, guys!

19
00:01:27,148 --> 00:01:28,315
Guys?

20
00:01:29,692 --> 00:01:30,859
Gyatso?

21
00:01:30,943 --> 00:01:32,611
Why did you disappear?

22
00:01:33,237 --> 00:01:34,738
I didn't mean to.

23
00:01:40,995 --> 00:01:43,080
We need you, Aang.

24
00:01:48,336 --> 00:01:50,587
We need you, Aang.
We need you.

25
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:53,715
We need you, Aang. We need you.

26
00:01:55,885 --> 00:01:57,636
What's going on?

27
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:58,970
Did we get captured again?

28
00:01:59,263 --> 00:02:01,431
It's nothing. I just had a bad dream.

29
00:02:01,557 --> 00:02:02,766
Go back to sleep.

30
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:03,934
You don't have to tell me twice.

31
00:02:04,644 --> 00:02:05,894
Are you all right, Aang?

32
00:02:05,978 --> 00:02:07,062
I'm okay.

33
00:02:07,271 --> 00:02:09,106
You seem to be having
a lot of nightmares lately.

34
00:02:09,190 --> 00:02:10,982
You want to tell me about it?

35
00:02:11,067 --> 00:02:12,818
I think I just need some rest.

36
00:02:12,902 --> 00:02:15,529
You guys want to hear about my dream?

37
00:02:16,114 --> 00:02:19,074
That's okay. I didn't want
to talk about it anyway.

38
00:02:24,163 --> 00:02:25,497
Look at those clear skies, buddy.

39
00:02:25,998 --> 00:02:27,582
Should be some smooth flying.

40
00:02:29,627 --> 00:02:32,629
Well, we'd better
smoothly fly ourselves to a market,

41
00:02:32,713 --> 00:02:33,922
because we're out of food.

42
00:02:34,132 --> 00:02:36,174
Guys, wait. This was in my dream.

43
00:02:36,259 --> 00:02:37,592
We shouldn't go to the market.

44
00:02:37,677 --> 00:02:38,718
What happened in your dream?

45
00:02:39,137 --> 00:02:40,804
Food eats people!

46
00:02:41,889 --> 00:02:44,266
Also, Momo could talk.

47
00:02:44,475 --> 00:02:46,309
You said some very unkind things.

48
00:02:53,651 --> 00:02:55,527
There is a storm coming.

49
00:02:55,736 --> 00:02:56,903
A big one.

50
00:02:57,113 --> 00:02:58,530
You're out of your mind, uncle.

51
00:02:58,614 --> 00:03:00,740
The weather is perfect.
There's not a cloud in sight.

52
00:03:01,534 --> 00:03:04,327
A storm is approaching from the north.

53
00:03:04,704 --> 00:03:08,498
I suggest we alter our course
and head southwest.

54
00:03:08,708 --> 00:03:10,417
We know the Avatar
is traveling northward,

55
00:03:10,501 --> 00:03:12,085
so we will do the same.

56
00:03:12,503 --> 00:03:15,297
Prince Zuko,
consider the safety of the crew.

57
00:03:15,506 --> 00:03:17,757
The safety of the crew doesn't matter.

58
00:03:21,179 --> 00:03:24,181
Finding the Avatar
is far more important

59
00:03:24,265 --> 00:03:26,224
than any individual's safety.

60
00:03:30,188 --> 00:03:33,648
He doesn't mean that.
He's just all worked up.

61
00:03:36,986 --> 00:03:39,488
It's good.
It's perfect, I'm telling you.

62
00:03:41,491 --> 00:03:43,700
I don't know if I like
the sound of that swishing.

63
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:45,327
Swishing means it's ripe.

64
00:03:45,536 --> 00:03:49,080
It's the ripe juices
swishing around?

65
00:03:49,290 --> 00:03:50,582
I think it's true, Katara.

66
00:03:50,666 --> 00:03:51,875
Swishing means it's ripe.

67
00:03:52,418 --> 00:03:54,294
I just realized
we're out of money, anyway.

68
00:03:55,505 --> 00:03:57,297
Aww...

69
00:04:00,885 --> 00:04:02,802
Out of food and out of money.

70
00:04:02,887 --> 00:04:04,304
Now what are we supposed to do?

71
00:04:04,514 --> 00:04:06,264
You could get a job, smart guy.

72
00:04:06,474 --> 00:04:07,724
We shouldn't go out there.

73
00:04:07,808 --> 00:04:09,768
Please! The fish can wait.

74
00:04:09,852 --> 00:04:11,686
There's going to be a terrible storm.

75
00:04:11,896 --> 00:04:14,356
Aw, you're crazy. It's a nice day.

76
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:16,483
No clouds, no wind, no nothing,

77
00:04:16,692 --> 00:04:18,485
so quit your nagging, woman.

78
00:04:18,694 --> 00:04:21,404
Maybe we should find some shelter.

79
00:04:21,614 --> 00:04:23,782
Are you kidding? Shelter from what?

80
00:04:23,991 --> 00:04:26,409
My joints say
there's going to be a storm,

81
00:04:26,494 --> 00:04:27,869
a bad one.

82
00:04:28,204 --> 00:04:30,914
Well, it's your joints
against my brain.

83
00:04:31,123 --> 00:04:33,625
Then I hope your brain can find
someone else to haul that fish,

84
00:04:33,709 --> 00:04:34,793
'cause I ain't coming!

85
00:04:35,002 --> 00:04:36,753
Then I'll find a new fish hauler,

86
00:04:36,837 --> 00:04:38,296
and pay him double what you get.

87
00:04:38,548 --> 00:04:39,548
How do you like that?

88
00:04:39,632 --> 00:04:40,632
I'll go.

89
00:04:40,716 --> 00:04:41,967
You're hired.

90
00:04:43,261 --> 00:04:45,220
What? You said get a job.

91
00:04:45,429 --> 00:04:46,721
And he's paying double.

92
00:04:46,889 --> 00:04:49,015
Double? Who told you that nonsense?

93
00:04:55,648 --> 00:04:59,067
Looks like your uncle was right
about the storm after all.

94
00:04:59,151 --> 00:05:00,277
Lucky guess.

95
00:05:00,361 --> 00:05:02,612
Lieutenant,
you'd better learn some respect,

96
00:05:03,281 --> 00:05:05,907
or I will teach it to you.

97
00:05:06,284 --> 00:05:08,577
What do you know about respect?

98
00:05:10,288 --> 00:05:12,789
The way you talk
to everyone around here,

99
00:05:12,999 --> 00:05:15,667
from your hard-working crew
to your esteemed uncle,

100
00:05:15,876 --> 00:05:18,962
shows you know nothing about respect.

101
00:05:19,171 --> 00:05:21,840
You don't care about
anyone but yourself.

102
00:05:22,049 --> 00:05:26,052
Then again, what should I expect
from a spoiled prince?

103
00:05:30,057 --> 00:05:31,266
Easy now.

104
00:05:34,770 --> 00:05:36,021
Enough!

105
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:40,358
We're all a bit tired
from being at sea so long.

106
00:05:40,943 --> 00:05:43,069
I'm sure after a bowl of noodles,

107
00:05:43,279 --> 00:05:46,156
everyone will feel much better.

108
00:05:48,951 --> 00:05:51,536
I don't need your help
keeping order on my ship.

109
00:06:00,129 --> 00:06:02,756
Sokka, maybe this isn't
such a good idea.

110
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:04,007
Look at the sky.

111
00:06:04,091 --> 00:06:05,634
I said I was gonna do this job.

112
00:06:05,718 --> 00:06:07,844
I can't back out just because
of some bad weather.

113
00:06:08,888 --> 00:06:11,264
The boy with the tattoos
has some sense.

114
00:06:11,349 --> 00:06:12,432
You should listen to him.

115
00:06:12,642 --> 00:06:14,768
Boy with tattoos?

116
00:06:14,977 --> 00:06:16,978
Airbender tattoos.

117
00:06:17,313 --> 00:06:20,023
Well, I'll be a hog monkey's uncle.

118
00:06:20,107 --> 00:06:21,524
You're the Avatar, ain't you?

119
00:06:21,817 --> 00:06:22,901
That's right.

120
00:06:23,152 --> 00:06:24,861
Well, don't be so smiley about it.

121
00:06:26,238 --> 00:06:28,740
The Avatar disappeared
for a hundred years!

122
00:06:28,991 --> 00:06:30,867
You turned your back on the world.

123
00:06:31,077 --> 00:06:32,744
Don't yell at him!

124
00:06:32,828 --> 00:06:34,913
Aang would never
turn his back on anyone.

125
00:06:35,164 --> 00:06:37,123
He wouldn't?

126
00:06:37,416 --> 00:06:39,042
Then I guess I must have imagined

127
00:06:39,126 --> 00:06:42,253
the last hundred years
of war and suffering.

128
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,923
Aang is the bravest person I know.

129
00:06:45,132 --> 00:06:46,925
He has done nothing but help people,

130
00:06:47,009 --> 00:06:49,260
and save lives since I met him.

131
00:06:49,470 --> 00:06:51,930
It's not his fault he disappeared,
right, Aang?

132
00:06:52,139 --> 00:06:53,682
Aang, what's wrong?

133
00:06:56,852 --> 00:06:58,895
That's right! Keep flying!

134
00:06:59,105 --> 00:07:00,689
You're a horrible old man!

135
00:07:05,111 --> 00:07:06,986
Appa, yip yip!

136
00:07:08,239 --> 00:07:10,407
Hey! They left
without saying good-bye.

137
00:07:10,616 --> 00:07:12,575
Your friends ain't too polite,
are they?

138
00:07:12,868 --> 00:07:14,703
I know. This one time, I was--

139
00:07:14,787 --> 00:07:16,705
Yeah, yeah, yeah. Get below deck.

140
00:07:37,143 --> 00:07:38,768
I'm sorry for running away.

141
00:07:38,853 --> 00:07:41,521
It's okay. That fisherman
was way out of line.

142
00:07:42,231 --> 00:07:44,065
Actually, he wasn't.

143
00:07:44,275 --> 00:07:46,651
What do you mean?

144
00:07:46,861 --> 00:07:48,528
I don't want to talk about it.

145
00:07:48,738 --> 00:07:51,281
It has to do with your dream,
doesn't it?

146
00:07:51,490 --> 00:07:52,907
Talk to me.

147
00:07:53,117 --> 00:07:55,410
Well, it's kind of a long story.

148
00:08:01,417 --> 00:08:03,710
I'm gonna try to get
a little fire going.

149
00:08:07,006 --> 00:08:09,924
I'll never forget the day
the monks told me I was the Avatar.

150
00:08:12,219 --> 00:08:15,221
I was playing with some other kids
just outside the south wall.

151
00:08:15,473 --> 00:08:17,891
I was trying to teach them
how to do the air scooter.

152
00:08:18,184 --> 00:08:21,394
First you form a ball.
Then you've got to get on quick.

153
00:08:23,189 --> 00:08:24,397
Ha ha ha!

154
00:08:24,607 --> 00:08:26,608
Yeah! Ha ha ha!

155
00:08:26,692 --> 00:08:28,276
Whoo-hoo! Yeah!

156
00:08:28,778 --> 00:08:31,237
Okay, here goes.

157
00:08:31,447 --> 00:08:32,447
Quick. Get on.

158
00:08:32,531 --> 00:08:34,991
Whoa. Whoa...

159
00:08:37,077 --> 00:08:39,162
You kind of have to balance on it
like it's a top.

160
00:08:39,371 --> 00:08:41,080
Man, that's hard.

161
00:08:41,290 --> 00:08:42,707
Where did you learn that trick, Aang?

162
00:08:42,875 --> 00:08:44,000
I made it up.

163
00:08:44,084 --> 00:08:45,627
Wow!

164
00:08:45,836 --> 00:08:47,796
Aang, come with us.

165
00:08:48,005 --> 00:08:49,798
We need to speak with you.

166
00:08:57,139 --> 00:08:58,723
How do you know it's me?

167
00:08:58,808 --> 00:09:02,143
We have known you were
the Avatar for some time.

168
00:09:02,728 --> 00:09:04,145
Do you remember these?

169
00:09:08,901 --> 00:09:11,653
Those were some of my favorite toys
when I was little.

170
00:09:11,862 --> 00:09:14,781
You chose them
from among thousands of toys, Aang.

171
00:09:15,157 --> 00:09:18,993
The toys you picked
were the four Avatar relics.

172
00:09:19,286 --> 00:09:22,163
These items belonged to Avatars past.

173
00:09:22,373 --> 00:09:24,415
Your own past lives.

174
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,584
I just chose them
because they seemed fun.

175
00:09:27,253 --> 00:09:29,796
You chose them
because they were familiar.

176
00:09:30,214 --> 00:09:34,634
Normally, we would have told you
of your identity when you turned 16.

177
00:09:35,010 --> 00:09:37,470
But there are troubling signs.

178
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:40,515
Storm clouds are gathering.

179
00:09:40,933 --> 00:09:44,435
I fear that war may be upon us,
young Avatar.

180
00:09:44,645 --> 00:09:46,145
We need you, Aang.

181
00:09:53,988 --> 00:09:55,905
I'm sick of taking his orders,

182
00:09:56,115 --> 00:09:58,032
and I'm tired of chasing his Avatar.

183
00:09:58,242 --> 00:10:00,535
I mean, who does Zuko think he is?

184
00:10:00,744 --> 00:10:02,495
Do you really want to know?

185
00:10:02,705 --> 00:10:04,497
General Iroh, we were just--

186
00:10:04,582 --> 00:10:06,124
It's okay.

187
00:10:06,333 --> 00:10:07,625
May I join you?

188
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:08,751
Of course, sir.

189
00:10:12,631 --> 00:10:14,299
Try to understand,

190
00:10:14,550 --> 00:10:16,926
my nephew is a complicated young man.

191
00:10:17,177 --> 00:10:19,012
He has been through much.

192
00:10:25,311 --> 00:10:26,519
Let me in!

193
00:10:26,604 --> 00:10:28,396
Prince Zuko, what's wrong?

194
00:10:28,606 --> 00:10:30,023
I want to go into the war chamber,

195
00:10:30,107 --> 00:10:31,858
but the guard won't let me pass.

196
00:10:31,942 --> 00:10:34,444
You're not missing anything. Trust me.

197
00:10:34,570 --> 00:10:37,447
These meetings are dreadfully boring.

198
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:39,741
If I'm going to rule
this nation one day,

199
00:10:39,825 --> 00:10:42,160
don't you think I need
to start learning as much as I can?

200
00:10:43,162 --> 00:10:46,873
Very well,
but you must promise not to speak.

201
00:10:47,207 --> 00:10:49,792
These old folks are a bit sensitive,
you know?

202
00:10:50,002 --> 00:10:52,086
Thank you, uncle.

203
00:10:58,344 --> 00:11:01,596
The Earth Kingdom defenses
are concentrated here,

204
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:04,307
a dangerous battalion
of their strongest earthbenders,

205
00:11:04,391 --> 00:11:06,184
and fiercest warriors.

206
00:11:06,518 --> 00:11:09,604
So, I am recommending
the 41st division.

207
00:11:09,813 --> 00:11:12,523
But the 41st is entirely new recruits.

208
00:11:12,733 --> 00:11:16,319
How do you expect them to defeat
a powerful Earth Kingdom battalion?

209
00:11:16,528 --> 00:11:18,571
I don't.

210
00:11:18,781 --> 00:11:20,323
They'll be used as a distraction

211
00:11:20,407 --> 00:11:22,325
while we mount an attack
from the rear.

212
00:11:22,785 --> 00:11:26,537
What better to use as bait
than fresh meat?

213
00:11:26,956 --> 00:11:29,290
You can't sacrifice
an entire division like that!

214
00:11:29,375 --> 00:11:31,501
Those soldiers love
and defend our nation.

215
00:11:31,585 --> 00:11:32,919
How can you betray them?

216
00:11:36,131 --> 00:11:37,757
Zuko was right, you see?

217
00:11:38,175 --> 00:11:41,135
But it was not his place to speak out.

218
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:43,930
And there were dire consequences.

219
00:11:46,892 --> 00:11:48,977
So you were upset
that you were the Avatar?

220
00:11:49,687 --> 00:11:51,521
Why wouldn't you be excited about it?

221
00:11:51,689 --> 00:11:54,107
Well, I didn't know
how to feel about it.

222
00:11:54,692 --> 00:11:56,401
All I knew was that after I found out,

223
00:11:56,735 --> 00:11:58,277
everything began changing.

224
00:11:59,196 --> 00:12:00,613
Hey, not bad.

225
00:12:00,698 --> 00:12:01,948
You guys have been practicing.

226
00:12:02,282 --> 00:12:03,658
Not only that,

227
00:12:03,742 --> 00:12:06,661
we made up a game you can play
with the air scooters.

228
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:07,954
Great!

229
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:13,835
What's going on?

230
00:12:14,211 --> 00:12:15,670
Now that you're the Avatar,

231
00:12:15,879 --> 00:12:17,505
it's kind of an unfair advantage

232
00:12:17,715 --> 00:12:19,090
for whichever team you're on.

233
00:12:19,299 --> 00:12:20,591
But I'm still the same.

234
00:12:20,801 --> 00:12:22,635
Nothing has changed.

235
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:25,263
So, what? I can't play?

236
00:12:25,472 --> 00:12:26,973
That's the only fair way.

237
00:12:27,182 --> 00:12:29,726
Okay...

238
00:12:29,810 --> 00:12:31,644
Sorry, Aang.

239
00:12:32,730 --> 00:12:35,398
Okay, now, who wants
to have Jinju on their team?

240
00:12:45,367 --> 00:12:48,036
Very interesting move, young one.

241
00:12:48,162 --> 00:12:49,787
What do you mean?

242
00:12:54,334 --> 00:12:56,502
Hey! Ha ha ha!

243
00:12:56,712 --> 00:12:59,005
Ha ha ha!

244
00:12:59,715 --> 00:13:01,049
You're playing games with him?

245
00:13:01,216 --> 00:13:03,384
The Avatar should be training.

246
00:13:03,594 --> 00:13:06,179
Aang has already
trained enough for today.

247
00:13:06,388 --> 00:13:08,514
Time is short. Come with me.

248
00:13:08,599 --> 00:13:11,392
I must test you
on some high-level techniques.

249
00:13:11,810 --> 00:13:14,228
No. As long as I am his guardian,

250
00:13:14,313 --> 00:13:16,314
I will decide when he trains

251
00:13:16,607 --> 00:13:19,192
And when he gets his butt kicked
at Pai Sho.

252
00:13:19,610 --> 00:13:20,860
Hmmph!

253
00:13:26,909 --> 00:13:30,203
After Zuko's outburst in the meeting,

254
00:13:30,287 --> 00:13:33,873
the Fire Lord became
very angry with him.

255
00:13:34,875 --> 00:13:38,086
He said that Prince Zuko's
challenge of the general

256
00:13:38,295 --> 00:13:42,215
was an act of complete disrespect.

257
00:13:42,424 --> 00:13:45,802
And there was only one way
to resolve this.

258
00:13:45,886 --> 00:13:48,596
Agni Kai. A fire duel.

259
00:13:48,931 --> 00:13:50,681
That's right.

260
00:13:50,766 --> 00:13:54,018
Zuko looked upon
the old general he had insulted,

261
00:13:54,103 --> 00:13:56,771
and declared that he was not afraid.

262
00:13:57,231 --> 00:13:59,774
But Zuko misunderstood.

263
00:13:59,983 --> 00:14:02,276
When he turned to face his opponent,

264
00:14:02,486 --> 00:14:05,613
he was surprised to see
it was not the general.

265
00:14:05,906 --> 00:14:09,742
Zuko had spoken out
against the general's plan,

266
00:14:09,827 --> 00:14:12,829
but by doing so
in the Fire Lord's war room,

267
00:14:13,038 --> 00:14:16,958
it was the Fire Lord
whom he had disrespected.

268
00:14:17,626 --> 00:14:22,421
Zuko would have to duel
his own father.

269
00:14:24,133 --> 00:14:26,676
Then, just when
I was starting to feel better,

270
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:28,553
something worse happened.

271
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:31,222
Aang needs to have freedom and fun.

272
00:14:31,431 --> 00:14:34,642
He needs to grow up as a normal boy.

273
00:14:34,810 --> 00:14:38,104
You cannot keep protecting him
from his destiny.

274
00:14:38,522 --> 00:14:41,023
Gyatso, I know you mean well,

275
00:14:41,233 --> 00:14:44,819
but you are letting your affection
for the boy cloud your judgment.

276
00:14:44,903 --> 00:14:48,489
All I want is what is best for him.

277
00:14:48,699 --> 00:14:51,826
But what we need
is what's best for the world.

278
00:14:54,621 --> 00:14:57,832
You and Aang must be separated.

279
00:14:57,916 --> 00:15:00,751
The Avatar will be sent away
to the Eastern Air Temple

280
00:15:00,961 --> 00:15:02,712
to complete his training.

281
00:15:13,473 --> 00:15:14,932
That's awful, Aang.

282
00:15:15,517 --> 00:15:17,351
I don't know what to say.

283
00:15:17,436 --> 00:15:19,061
How could they do that to me?

284
00:15:19,146 --> 00:15:20,688
They wanted to take away
everything I knew,

285
00:15:20,772 --> 00:15:22,023
and everyone I loved!

286
00:15:22,232 --> 00:15:24,150
Whoa! Hot cinders.

287
00:15:25,485 --> 00:15:27,320
I'm sorry I got so mad.

288
00:15:27,863 --> 00:15:29,238
You have a right to be angry

289
00:15:29,323 --> 00:15:30,781
after the monks
sent you away like that.

290
00:15:31,241 --> 00:15:33,868
Well, that's not exactly
what happened.

291
00:15:39,082 --> 00:15:41,250
I was afraid and confused.

292
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:43,294
I didn't know what to do.

293
00:15:49,301 --> 00:15:51,177
Aang?

294
00:15:51,261 --> 00:15:53,763
I'm not going to let them
take you away from me.

295
00:15:53,972 --> 00:15:55,139
Aang?

296
00:16:03,357 --> 00:16:05,650
I never saw Gyatso again.

297
00:16:21,375 --> 00:16:23,542
Next thing I knew,
I was waking up in your arms

298
00:16:23,627 --> 00:16:25,753
after you found me in the iceberg.

299
00:16:29,091 --> 00:16:30,216
You ran away.

300
00:16:30,592 --> 00:16:33,052
And then the Fire Nation
attacked our temple.

301
00:16:33,136 --> 00:16:35,221
My people needed me,
and I wasn't there to help.

302
00:16:35,597 --> 00:16:36,973
You don't know what would have--

303
00:16:37,057 --> 00:16:38,808
The world needed me,
and I wasn't there to help.

304
00:16:39,142 --> 00:16:41,018
-Aang...
-The fisherman was right.

305
00:16:41,311 --> 00:16:42,895
I did turn my back on the world.

306
00:16:43,355 --> 00:16:45,398
You're being too hard on yourself.

307
00:16:45,482 --> 00:16:46,857
Even if you did run away,

308
00:16:47,192 --> 00:16:49,026
I think it was meant to be.

309
00:16:49,403 --> 00:16:50,987
If you had stayed,
you would have been killed

310
00:16:51,071 --> 00:16:52,780
along with all the other airbenders.

311
00:16:53,031 --> 00:16:54,407
You don't know that.

312
00:16:54,491 --> 00:16:56,534
I know it's meant to be this way.

313
00:16:56,994 --> 00:16:59,954
The world needs you now.

314
00:17:00,038 --> 00:17:01,289
You give people hope.

315
00:17:07,587 --> 00:17:10,339
When Prince Zuko saw
that it was his father

316
00:17:10,424 --> 00:17:12,383
who had come to duel him,

317
00:17:12,509 --> 00:17:14,051
he begged for mercy.

318
00:17:15,971 --> 00:17:17,263
Please, father,

319
00:17:17,347 --> 00:17:19,348
I only had the Fire Nation's
best interests at heart.

320
00:17:19,558 --> 00:17:20,933
I'm sorry I spoke out of turn.

321
00:17:21,435 --> 00:17:24,186
You will fight for your honor.

322
00:17:24,730 --> 00:17:26,522
I meant you no disrespect.

323
00:17:26,606 --> 00:17:27,857
I am your loyal son.

324
00:17:28,191 --> 00:17:31,360
Rise and fight, Prince Zuko.

325
00:17:31,445 --> 00:17:33,112
I won't fight you.

326
00:17:33,363 --> 00:17:35,656
You will learn respect,

327
00:17:36,158 --> 00:17:39,618
and suffering will be your teacher.

328
00:17:41,538 --> 00:17:43,706
I looked away.

329
00:17:48,795 --> 00:17:52,965
I always thought that Prince Zuko
was in a training accident.

330
00:17:53,133 --> 00:17:55,760
It was no accident.

331
00:17:56,136 --> 00:17:57,762
After the duel,

332
00:17:57,846 --> 00:18:01,349
the Fire Lord said
that by refusing to fight,

333
00:18:02,059 --> 00:18:04,977
Zuko had shown shameful weakness.

334
00:18:05,395 --> 00:18:07,646
As punishment, he was banished,

335
00:18:07,731 --> 00:18:10,816
and sent to capture the Avatar.

336
00:18:11,234 --> 00:18:14,904
Only then could he return
with his honor.

337
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:18,032
So that's why he's so obsessed.

338
00:18:18,325 --> 00:18:20,743
Capturing the Avatar
is the only chance he has

339
00:18:20,827 --> 00:18:23,079
of things returning to normal.

340
00:18:23,246 --> 00:18:25,331
Things will never return to normal,

341
00:18:25,499 --> 00:18:27,958
but the important thing is,

342
00:18:28,168 --> 00:18:30,544
the Avatar gives Zuko hope.

343
00:18:47,396 --> 00:18:50,106
Help! Please, help!

344
00:18:50,482 --> 00:18:52,483
It's okay. You're safe.

345
00:18:52,567 --> 00:18:54,360
But my husband isn't.

346
00:18:54,444 --> 00:18:56,612
What do you mean? Where's Sokka?

347
00:18:56,863 --> 00:18:58,280
They haven't returned.

348
00:18:58,365 --> 00:18:59,907
They should have been back by now.

349
00:19:00,033 --> 00:19:02,243
And this storm is becoming a typhoon.

350
00:19:02,494 --> 00:19:04,078
They're caught out at sea!

351
00:19:04,371 --> 00:19:05,704
I'm going to find them.

352
00:19:05,914 --> 00:19:06,956
I'm going with you.

353
00:19:07,165 --> 00:19:08,249
I'm staying here.

354
00:19:11,128 --> 00:19:13,587
We'll be back soon. I promise.

355
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:21,387
Where were we hit?

356
00:19:21,471 --> 00:19:22,471
I don't know.

357
00:19:22,556 --> 00:19:24,390
Look!

358
00:19:24,975 --> 00:19:26,267
The helmsman!

359
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,326
Aah!

360
00:19:54,463 --> 00:19:55,796
Where are they?

361
00:19:58,925 --> 00:20:00,926
Come on, Appa!

362
00:20:11,897 --> 00:20:13,689
The boat! There!

363
00:20:16,318 --> 00:20:17,693
The Avatar!

364
00:20:17,777 --> 00:20:20,362
What do you want to do, sir?

365
00:20:20,447 --> 00:20:21,989
Let him go.

366
00:20:22,073 --> 00:20:23,991
We need to get this ship to safety.

367
00:20:24,201 --> 00:20:28,078
Then we must head directly
into the eye of the storm.

368
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:38,631
I'm too young to die!

369
00:20:38,715 --> 00:20:40,508
I'm not, but I still don't want to!

370
00:20:55,774 --> 00:20:57,024
Hang on to the rope!

371
00:21:01,446 --> 00:21:02,988
Whoa! Whoa!

372
00:21:50,036 --> 00:21:52,413
Uncle, I am sorry.

373
00:21:52,831 --> 00:21:54,915
Your apology is accepted.

374
00:22:15,729 --> 00:22:17,813
You're alive!

375
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:20,357
You owe this boy an apology.

376
00:22:20,442 --> 00:22:22,276
He doesn't have to apologize.

377
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:25,154
What if, instead of an apology,

378
00:22:25,238 --> 00:22:27,656
I give him a free fish,
and we call it even?

379
00:22:27,866 --> 00:22:29,617
Actually, I don't eat meat.

380
00:22:29,743 --> 00:22:31,076
Fish ain't meat.

381
00:22:31,494 --> 00:22:33,621
Seriously, you're still gonna pay me,
right?

382
00:22:34,914 --> 00:22:35,914
Aah!

383
00:22:36,166 --> 00:22:38,042
Katara, I think you were right before.

384
00:22:38,293 --> 00:22:39,585
I'm done dwelling on the past.

385
00:22:39,669 --> 00:22:40,794
Really?

386
00:22:41,004 --> 00:22:43,047
I can't make guesses about
how things would have turned out

387
00:22:43,131 --> 00:22:44,340
If I hadn't run away.

388
00:22:45,050 --> 00:22:46,967
I'm here now, and I'm going
to make the most of it.

389
00:22:47,344 --> 00:22:49,637
I don't think you're gonna have
those nightmares anymore.

390
00:22:50,639 --> 00:22:52,431
If you weren't here now...

391
00:22:52,557 --> 00:22:54,975
Well, I guess, I wouldn't be either.

392
00:22:55,185 --> 00:22:57,728
Thank you for saving my life, Avatar.

393
00:22:59,564 --> 00:23:01,357
Do you hear that?

394
00:23:01,441 --> 00:23:02,441
It stopped raining.

395
00:23:09,741 --> 00:23:11,867
Appa!
